      "fTerm": "ELECTROTHERAPY; MAGNETOTHERAPY; RADIATION THERAPY; ULTRASOUND THERAPY (measurement of bioelectric currents <b>A61B</b>; surgical instruments, devices or methods for transferring non-mechanical forms of energy to or from the body <b>A61B 18/00</b>; anaesthetic apparatus in general <b>A61M</b>; incandescent lamps <b>H01K</b>; infrared radiators for heating <b>H05B</b>)<b>[6]</b><br><br><b><u>Note(s)</u></b><br><br><ul type=\"\"1\"\"><li>In this subclass, the following term is used with the meaning indicated:<b>[5,7]</b><ul type=\"\"disc\"\"><li>&quot;therapy&quot; implies that the treatment, when it aims at destroying sick or abnormal cells, is performed within the limits of healthy cell life, the destruction thereof being undesired, contrary to that which takes place with instruments, devices or methods covered by group <b>A61B 18/00</b>.</li></ul></li></ul><br><br><b><u>Subclass indexes</u></b><br><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">ELECTROTHERAPY</td><td><b>1/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">MAGNETOTHERAPY</td><td><b>2/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">RADIATION THERAPY</td><td><b>5/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">ULTRASOUND THERAPY</td><td><b>7/00</b></td></p></tr></table>",
